// `typeid` takes a TYPE. Passing a VALUE must be rejected, and the diagnostic
// must name an API that EXISTS: it used to suggest `is()`, which the language
// has never had (issues/fixed/typeid-diagnostic-suggests-a-nonexistent-is-builtin.md).
main :: (fn() -> unit)({
  x := i32(1);
  y := typeid(x);
  ()
});
export(main);
